{
  "source": "us-gaap tag candidates per canonical field, verified against the universe's SEC XBRL companyfacts on 2026-09-19; selection is per fiscal period because tags change between years (Apple's Revenues stops at FY2018, Microsoft's at FY2010, Allstate's IncurredClaimsPropertyCasualtyAndLiability at FY2023, Coca-Cola's LongTermDebt at FY2023)",
  "as_of": "2026-09-19",
  "notes": [
    "Only annual facts: form in annual_forms with fp = FY; a duration fact must span annual_span_days because fp = FY also marks quarters; a balance must carry no start; the latest filing wins per fiscal year end.",
    "A canonical field the map cannot supply for a period stays null and the valuation fails naming it; there is no per-field fallback to the vendor feed.",
    "depreciation_amortization: the aggregate tags first; when none is filed, Depreciation plus AmortizationOfIntangibleAssets where filed (Microsoft and Alphabet file only these), labelled as the sum.",
    "total_debt: the first complete recipe, plus DebtCurrent where filed; LongTermDebt already includes the current portion of long-term debt, and commercial paper is not included, so the vendor's total debt will usually read higher; the cross-check records it.",
    "delta_nwc: year-over-year change in (current assets - cash) - (current liabilities - current debt where filed), from the balance sheets; filers rarely tag the aggregate working-capital line.",
    "cash is cash and equivalents only; the vendor's canonical cash includes short-term investments, so the cross-check will flag cash-rich names.",
    "cross_check_threshold 0.02 is an assumption: two providers reading the same filing should agree to within rounding; a larger gap is a definitional difference worth reading."
  ],
  "cross_check_threshold": 0.02,
  "max_filing_age_days": 400,
  "annual_forms": [
    "10-K",
    "10-K/A"
  ],
  "annual_span_days": [
    350,
    380
  ],
